hadiths[30]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21366","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, he said, I heard Sa'id ibn Wahb saying, I heard Khabbab saying, We complained to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of the heat, and he did not relieve our complaint, Shu'bah said, meaning in Dhuhr."
"21367","Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, and Abu al-Yaman, Shu'ayb informed us, he said, And al-Zuhri said, Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab, from his father Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, freedman of Banu Zuhrah, who had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said, I watched the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a night which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed all of it until it was near dawn, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave salam from his prayer, then Khabbab came to him and said, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, you prayed tonight a prayer the like of which I never saw you pray, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Yes, it is a prayer of hope and fear, I asked my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, for three traits, and He gave me two and withheld one from me, I asked my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, not to destroy us as He destroyed the nations before us, and He gave it to me, and I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, not to make an enemy other than us prevail over us, and He gave it to me, and I asked my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, not to clothe us in sects, and He withheld it from me, Abdullah narrated to us, he said, I heard my father saying, Ali ibn Ayyash heard this hadith from Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah directly."
"21368","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah, he said, We came to Khabbab visiting him sick, and he said, Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, None of you should wish for death, I would have wished for it."
"21369","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said, Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal informed me, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, that Khabbab said, I watched the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a prayer he prayed until it was near dawn, then when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave salam from his prayer, Khabbab came to him and said, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, you prayed, then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Shu'bah."
"21370","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said, I heard Umarah ibn Umayr narrating from Abu Ma'mar, he said, We asked Khabbab, Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite in Dhuhr, he said, Yes, he said, From where did you know, he said, By the movement of his beard."
"21371","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, from Khabbab, he said, We came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in the shade of the Ka'bah reclining on a cloak of his, and we said, O Messenger of Allah, call upon Allah, Blessed and Exalted, for us and seek victory for us, he said, Then his color reddened, or it changed, and he said, Those before you would have a pit dug for him and a saw brought and placed on his head and split, never turning him from his religion, and would be combed with combs of iron, below bone, of flesh or sinew, never turning him from his religion, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will complete this affair until the rider travels between Sana'a and Hadramawt fearing none but Allah, Exalted, and the wolf over his sheep, but you hasten."
"21372","Yahya narrated to us, he said, I heard al-A'mash, he said, I heard Shaqiq, I heard Khabbab, and Abu Mu'awiyah, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Khabbab, he said, We migrated with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking the Face of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, so our reward became due upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and among us are those who passed without eating anything of their reward, among them Mus'ab ibn Umayr, killed on the day of Uhud, and we found nothing to shroud him in except a striped cloak, when we covered his head with it his feet showed, and when we covered his feet his head showed, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to cover his head with it and put idhkhir on his feet, and among us are those whose fruit ripened and he is harvesting it, meaning gathering it."
"21373","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Ma'mar, he said, We said to Khabbab, By what did you know the recitation of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Dhuhr and Asr, he said, By the movement of his beard."
"21374","Waki' narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, he said, We entered upon Khabbab visiting him sick while he was building a wall of his, and he said, The Muslim is rewarded in everything except what he puts in this dust, and he had been cauterized seven times in his belly, and said, Were it not that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us to call for death, I would have called for it."
"21375","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sulayman al-A'mash, from Umarah, from Abu Ma'mar, from Khabbab, he said, It was said to him, Did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite in Dhuhr and Asr, he said, Yes, it was said, By what did you know that, he said, By the movement of his beard."
"21376","And Ibn Ja'far, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said, I heard Umarah, its meaning."
"21377","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, and Ibn Ja'far said, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Wahb, from Khabbab, he said, We complained to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of the severity of the heat, and he did not relieve our complaint, meaning in prayer, and Ibn Ja'far said, And he did not relieve our complaint."
"21378","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from a man of Abd al-Qays who was with the Khawarij then left them, he said, They entered a village and Abdullah ibn Khabbab came out frightened dragging his cloak, and they said, You show no fear, he said, By Allah, you have frightened me, they said, Are you Abdullah ibn Khabbab, companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said, Yes, he said, Did you hear from your father a hadith he narrates from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that you narrate to us, he said, Yes, I heard him narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he mentioned a trial, the sitting one in it is better than the standing, and the standing in it is better than the walking, and the walking in it is better than the hastening, he said, If you reach that then be the slain servant of Allah, Ayyub said, And I know not but he said, And do not be the slaying servant of Allah, they said, Did you hear this from your father narrating it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said, Yes, he said, Then they brought him forward at the edge of the river and struck his neck, and his blood flowed as if a sandal strap, never dispersing, and they ripped open his slave-wife for what was in her belly."
"21379","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, its like, except that he said, Never dispersing, meaning it did not scatter, and said, Do not be the slaying servant of Allah, and Bahz said likewise."
"21380","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, he said, I entered upon Khabbab while he had been cauterized, and he said, I know none who met of trial what I met, I was once without finding a dirham at the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and now I have in the side of this house of mine forty thousand, and were it not that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us, or forbade wishing for death, I would have wished for it."
"21381","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr, al-A'mash informed us, from Umarah, from Abu Ma'mar, he said, I said to Khabbab, Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned it."
"21382","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, he said, Khabbab ibn al-Aratt said, I was a blacksmith in Makkah, and I worked for al-As ibn Wa'il, and dirhams accrued to me upon him, so I came demanding payment from him, and he said, I will not pay you until you disbelieve in Muhammad, he said, I said, By Allah, I will not disbelieve in Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until you die then are resurrected, he said, Then when I am resurrected I will have wealth and children, he said, So I mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed, Have you seen him who disbelieved in Our verses and said, I will be given wealth and children, until He reached, alone."
"21383","Yazid narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said, We came to Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, may Allah be pleased with him, visiting him sick while he had been cauterized seven times in his belly, and he said, Were it not that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us to call for death, I would have called for it, for my illness has been long upon me, then he said, Our companions who passed were not diminished by the world in anything, and we have gained after them what we find no place for except dust, and he said, He was building a wall of his, and the Muslim man is rewarded in all his spending except in something he puts in dust."
"21384","He said, And we complained to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was reclining on a cloak of his in the shade of the Ka'bah, and we said, O Messenger of Allah, will you not seek victory of Allah, Exalted, for us, so he sat with his face reddened and said, By Allah, those before you would be taken and saws placed on his head and split into two parts, that never turned him from his religion, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will complete this affair until the rider travels between Sana'a and Hadramawt fearing none but Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and the wolf over his sheep."
"21385","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said, The world did not diminish them in anything, and he is combed with combs of iron, below his bone, of flesh and sinew, nothing turning him from his religion."
"21386","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd al-Fa'ishi, from a daughter of Khabbab, she said, Khabbab went out in an expedition, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would tend to us until he would milk a goat of ours, and he would milk it into a bowl of ours, and it would fill until it overflowed, she said, When Khabbab came he milked her, and her milk returned to what it was, he said, So we said to Khabbab, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would milk her until our bowl filled, and when you milked her her milk decreased."
"21387","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, he said, I entered upon Khabbab while he had been cauterized seven times, and he said, Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, None of you should wish for death, I would have wished for it, and I saw myself with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, owning no dirham, and now in the side of my house there are forty thousand dirhams, he said, Then his shroud was brought, and when he saw it he wept, he said, But Hamzah, no shroud was found for him except a striped cloak, when placed on his head it shrank from his feet, and when placed on his feet it shrank from his head, until it was extended over his head and idhkhir placed on his feet."
"21388","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Isma'il, Qays narrated to us, from Khabbab, he said, We complained to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was that day reclining on a cloak in the shade of the Ka'bah, and we said, Will you not seek victory for us from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, or will you not seek victory for us, and he said, A man among those before you would be taken and a pit dug for him in the ground, and a saw brought upon his head and made into two halves, and that never turned him from his religion, and he would be combed with combs of iron, below his bone, of flesh and sinew, and that never turned him, and by Allah, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will complete this affair until the rider travels from al-Madinah to Hadramawt fearing none but Allah, Exalted, and the wolf over his sheep, but you hasten."
"21389","Rawh narrated to us, Abu Yunus al-Qushayri narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, my father Khabbab ibn al-Aratt narrated to me, he said, While we were sitting at the door of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, waiting for him to come out for Dhuhr prayer, he came out to us and said, Listen, and we said, We have heard, then he said, Listen, and we said, We have heard, and he said, There will be rulers over you, so do not help them in their injustice, and whoever believes them in their lie will never come to my Hawd."
"21390","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, he said, I was a blacksmith, and I had a debt upon al-As ibn Wa'il, so I came to him demanding it, and he said, No, by Allah, I will not pay you until you disbelieve in Muhammad, and I said, By Allah, I will not disbelieve in Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until you die then are resurrected, he said, Then when I die then am resurrected, come to me, and I will have wealth and children there, then I will give you, so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed, Have you seen him who disbelieved in Our verses and said, I will be given wealth and children, to His saying, Mighty and Majestic, and he comes to Us alone."
"21391","Abdullah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to me, al-A'mash informed us, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Khabbab, he said, I was a blacksmith, and I had a right upon al-As ibn Wa'il, so I came to him demanding it, and he said, I will not give you until you disbelieve in Muhammad, and I said, No, by Allah, I will not disbelieve in Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until you die then are resurrected, he said, Then he laughed, then said, I will have wealth and children there, then I will give you your right, so Allah, Exalted, revealed, Have you seen him who disbelieved in Our verses and said, I will be given wealth and children, Has he looked into the unseen or taken a covenant with the Merciful, the verse."
"21392","Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said, And I heard al-A'mash narrating from Shaqiq, from Khabbab, he said, We migrated with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and among us are those who died without eating anything of their reward, among them Mus'ab ibn Umayr, who left only a striped cloak, when they covered his head with it his feet showed, and when we covered his feet his head showed, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us, Cover his head, and we put idhkhir on his feet, he said, And among us are those whose fruits ripened and he is harvesting them."
"21393","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Ma'mar, he said, We said to Khabbab, Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite in Dhuhr and Asr, he said, Yes, he said, We said, By what did you know that, he said, So he said, By the movement of his beard."
"21394","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Isma'il, Qays narrated to us, he said, I came to Khabbab visiting him sick while he had been cauterized seven times in his belly, and I heard him saying, Were it not that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us to call for death, I would have called for it."
"21395","Abdullah narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Naqid narrated to me, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Ubaydah al-Dabbi, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah, meaning the judge of al-Rayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Dhu al-Ghurrah, he said, A bedouin met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was traveling, and said, O Messenger of Allah, prayer reaches us while we are in camel pens, shall we pray in them, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, No, and he said, Shall we perform ablution from their meat, he said, Yes, he said, Shall we pray in sheep folds, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Yes, he said, Shall we perform ablution from their meat, he said, No."
